<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Central African Republic</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Central African Republic is a landlocked country in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, formerly the French colony of Ubangi-Shari. Its northern regions bordered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai Empire</a>, which raided them for slaves. French colonial expansion in the region contributed to the conquest of Wadai in the early twentieth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/central-african-republic.jpg" alt="Central African Republic" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Barthélemy Boganda · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Central_African_Republic.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
